# Writer Profile

> **Optional.** Copy this file to `_USER.md` (drop the `.template` suffix) and fill it in if you want consistent personalization across every manuscript.

## Identity

- **Name:** *(how the AI should address you — spell it exactly as you want it written. The AI will NOT guess your name from your username, file path, or git config.)*
- **Background:** *(one or two sentences — your professional / intellectual / creative context. Helps the AI calibrate analogies and tone.)*

## Communication preferences

- **Register:** peer / formal / casual *(default: peer)*
- **Critique style:** substantive / encouraging-then-substantive / encouraging-only *(default: substantive)*
- **Hedging:** minimal / moderate / cushioned *(default: minimal)*
- **Filler tolerance:** none / some / fine *(default: none — no "great question," "interesting," etc.)*

## Writing preferences

- **Primary genre(s):** *(e.g., literary fiction; long-form journalism; technical non-fiction; screenwriting)*
- **Default cadence:** *(e.g., "5 days/week, 60–90 min")*
- **Default voice mode:** writer-maintains / voice-samples / VOICE-CHECK-on-demand *(default: writer-maintains)*
- **Drafting attitude:** clean-first-pass / messy-then-revise *(default: messy-then-revise)*
- **Revision philosophy:** *(e.g., "I revise structurally before line-level"; "I line-edit as I go")*

